THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

An MIT licence on this code does not and cannot alter anyone else's terms.
Full notices are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, which is part of the release rather
than documentation: the Dockerfile redistributes some of what it lists, and an
attribution obligation is not discharged by a comment nobody ships.

Exactly one component here is third-party. data/sap_baseline_requirements.json
is derived from SAP-samples/frun-csa-policies-best-practices, which is
Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2020 SAP SE or an SAP affiliate company. Identifiers,
titles, tiers and configuration-store names are taken; SAP's prose is not
reproduced and SAP's SQL predicates are neither copied nor executed. The licence
text is at licenses/Apache-2.0.txt, and the derived file carries its source,
licence and copyright in its own _meta block so the notice travels with the
data.

That notice is required by Apache-2.0 and stays regardless of the licence on
this project.
